{#-
  Tells somebody that the feedback they sent has a reply. It says so and
  links to their feedback page.

  Never the reply, and never what they wrote. Either may hold patient
  data, so both stay in Quill, one press away. Context:
    url  the link to their own feedback page
-#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_components.html.j2" as c with context %}
{% block subject %}Your feedback has a reply{% endblock %}
{% block preheader %}Open Quill to read it.{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
{{ c.heading("Your feedback has a *reply*") }}
{{ c.paragraph("Thank you for telling us. We have replied to the feedback you sent through Quill.") }}
{{ c.button("Read the reply", url) }}
{{ c.small("The reply is not in this email. It stays in Quill, where only you and our team can read it.") }}
{% endblock %}
{% block reason %}You are receiving this because you sent feedback on Quill.{% endblock %}

{% block text %}
Thank you for telling us. We have replied to the feedback you sent through Quill.

Read the reply: {{ url }}

The reply is not in this email. It stays in Quill, where only you and our team can read it.
{% endblock %}
